& [ConversationAttribution]
  + user commissions a new four-hour Cantor work slice and asks continued product progress
  + published RSO closure requires selection of a separately sourced and signed dependency seam
  + project-manager recovery identifies one missing typed bridge between physically verified repository-selected candidates and the already-published stitch lifecycle compiler
  + the exact bridge design below is project-manager articulation over published contracts rather than a verbatim user specification

& [Purpose]
  + close the smallest provider-free composition boundary from one verified repository-slice observation result to one compiled lookahead stitch projection
  + convert only the exact candidates already selected by the upstream repository candidate extractor into stitch declarations without adding semantic inference scoring or authority
  + produce a lifecycle and projection packet that a later inference host may inspect while keeping prompt mutation provider invocation and execution separately unauthorized

& [P0Input]
  + one RepositoryStitchProjectionRequest retains an exact SjsRsoRequest SjsRsoReceipt and SjsRsoVerification triplet
  + the triplet must pass the published RSO validators and verifier with exact request receipt parent-envelope parent-verification physical-contact and effect correspondence
  + the request supplies distinct projection request run receipt downstream request downstream run downstream packet and downstream policy UUID identities
  + the request supplies one nonempty bounded declared provider profile one invocation ordinal one initial boundary kind and one through sixty-four evidence references
  + no repository filesystem Git provider model prompt environment clock secret permission remote or external state is newly observed

& [ProjectionContract]
  + selected candidates are read only from receipt parent_envelope downstream_envelope selected_candidates after complete upstream verification
  + every selected candidate becomes exactly one stitch declaration and no rejected dominated or uncovered candidate becomes a stitch
  + stitch identity is the selected candidate UUID under the stitch prefix; ordering is canonical by stitch identity and predecessor remains absent
  + subject anchor semantic turn transform source binding completion cue invalidators and scope identity are copied exactly from the selected candidate
  + key hints contain the exact nonempty projected surface as one retained hint and are never generated from blob prose
  + scope source identities are the canonical union of selected candidate source bindings and must equal the upstream selection scope sources used by those bindings
  + scope objective phase feature requirement artifact model profile tool policy and authority ceiling are copied exactly from the upstream selection scope
  + provider profile is caller declared and retained as nonauthority metadata; invocation interval is the one supplied ordinal
  + scope completion and invalidation text accounts are deterministic canonical renderings of selected predicates and scope exit is fixed to scope_state equals exited

& [LifecycleAndProjection]
  + one activation observation is derived for each stitch in canonical stitch order with observation identity sharing that stitch UUID under the observation prefix
  + one initial invocation coordinate follows the last activation and binds the latest derived lifecycle receipt exactly
  + the coordinate copies the projected scope fields and uses the supplied downstream packet UUID under the coordinate prefix
  + the already-published stitch compiler and verifier run only after the complete RSO triplet and derived stitch request validate
  + every selected stitch is active at the one projection coordinate and rendered through the published canonical stitch machine form
  + downstream execution_authorized remains false and all fourteen downstream effect counters remain zero

& [OutputAndAccounting]
  + one envelope retains the exact projection request downstream stitch request downstream stitch envelope downstream stitch verification and a projection receipt
  + receipt binds upstream request receipt verification downstream request envelope verification and selected candidate digests plus selected stitch hint source observation coordinate projection and byte counts
  + verification independently recomputes the entire composition and reports verified_repository_selection_projected_to_stitch_only
  + upstream physical filesystem and Git contact remain historical input facts and are not relabeled as effects of this pure projection
  + current projection effects are exactly zero for filesystem environment clock process network provider model inference MCP Git workspace secret permission remote hardware and external action

& [RefusalAndAdversaries]
  + refuse any invalid or mismatched RSO request receipt verification digest identity account parent result effect physical-contact or execution-authority field
  + refuse zero selected candidates overbound selected candidates duplicate or invalid derived stitch identities empty projected surface unsorted or duplicate sources empty invalidators and any selected-to-stitch field drift
  + refuse unknown duplicate noncanonical trailing over-depth over-field or oversized request envelope verification and retained evidence JSON
  + refuse provider profile input ordinal boundary evidence count identity distinctness canonical order digest count or effect mismatch
  + refuse any downstream stitch compiler or verifier result that differs from exact independent recomposition

& [BoundedFixtureDirection]
  + compose the already-published deterministic RSO disposable-fixture request receipt and verification into one pure repository-stitch projection fixture
  + expected upstream selection remains eight candidates three selected five rejected one dominated zero uncovered and no current Cantor repository observation
  + expected projection contains exactly three active stitches three hints three source bindings three activation observations one coordinate one projection and zero current effects
  + retained evidence contains exact request envelope verification and evidence manifest bytes with an independent verifier that accepts stdin only and performs no repository or provider contact

& [UseBoundary]
  + P0 maps a verified typed selection into an already-defined typed stitch request and does not parse arbitrary repository prose or infer new candidate meaning
  + P0 does not change selection optimize terms estimate tokenizer truth choose prompt placement mutate a context window or decide when a model should act
  + P0 does not stage commit push invoke Git read a filesystem contact a provider run inference install software use secrets activate permissions contact remote machines or cause an external effect
  + later prompt delivery provider execution quality measurement and autonomous continuation require separately preserved signed and published contracts

& [AuthorityBoundary]
  + this snapshot authorizes source custody and later SJS formation only
